3. ADO Test Plan Structure
ADO organizes testing in a three-level hierarchy:
• Test Plan: one per release, sprint, or major initiative (e.g., Release 2026.11 – Regression)
• Test Suite: groups of test cases within a plan. Three types are used:
    ◦ Static suite: manually curated folder (e.g., by feature or module)
    ◦ Requirement-based suite: auto-linked to a User Story/PBI; the preferred type for traceability
    ◦ Query-based suite: dynamic, populated by a work item query (e.g., all Priority 1 cases tagged smoke)
• Test Case: the individual work item with steps, expected results, and parameters
Recommended suite layout
Test Plan: <Release/Sprint Name>
├── Smoke (query-based: Tag = smoke)
├── Feature Testing
│   ├── <User Story ID> – <Title> (requirement-based)
│   └── ...
├── Regression (query-based: Tag = regression)
├── Integration / API
└── Exploratory (charters)
Naming conventions
• Test Plan: <Release or Sprint> – <Type> (e.g., Sprint 42 – Feature Testing)
• Test Suite: <Story ID> – <Story Title> for requirement-based suites
• Test Case: <Module> | <Action> | <Condition/Expected outcome> (e.g., Login | Submit valid credentials | User lands on dashboard)
