5. Authoring and Review Workflow
1. Story refinement: QA reviews acceptance criteria and raises gaps before the sprint starts.
2. Create the suite: in Test Plans → Test Plans, open the plan and add a requirement-based suite for the story (or use Add existing user story).
3. Author cases: add test cases from the suite grid or the Test Case work item form. State = Design.
4. Link: confirm each case is linked to the story (auto-linked in requirement-based suites).
5. Peer review: a second QA or the developer reviews for accuracy, coverage, and clarity; comments are captured on the work item Discussion.
6. Approve: reviewer moves State to Ready. Cases in Design are excluded from execution runs.
7. Assign: assign testers and configurations in the suite's Execute tab.
Review checklist
[ ] Title follows naming convention
[ ] Linked to a story and mapped to acceptance criteria
[ ] Steps are atomic with clear expected results
[ ] Positive, negative, and boundary scenarios covered
[ ] Test data and preconditions defined
[ ] Priority, tags, and automation status set
[ ] Shared steps and parameters used where applicable
