7. Executing Test Cases
7.1 Execution steps
1. Open Test Plans → Execute and select the plan and suite.
2. Filter by tester, configuration, or outcome as needed.
3. Select a test point and choose Run for web application (or Run with options to pick the build and runner).
4. In the Test Runner, mark each step Pass or Fail. Steps marked Fail prompt for a comment.
5. Capture evidence: screenshots, screen recordings, or action logs from the runner.
6. Set the overall outcome and Save and close.
7.2 Outcome definitions
Outcome
Use when
Passed
All steps met expected results
Failed
One or more steps did not meet expected results; a defect is logged
Blocked
Cannot proceed due to an external issue (environment down, upstream defect); note the blocker
Not Applicable
Case does not apply for this configuration or release
Not Run
Not yet executed
7.3 Logging defects from the runner
1. On a failed step, select Create bug in the Test Runner. ADO pre-fills repro steps, build, configuration, and attachments.
2. Set Severity, Priority, Area/Iteration, and assign to the owning developer.
3. Confirm the bug is linked to the test case and the story.
4. Add a clear title in the form <Module> – <Observed behavior>.
7.4 Retesting and regression
• When a bug is resolved, the tester re-executes the failed test point against the fixed build and updates the outcome.
• Reset outcomes for a new cycle with Reset test to active (or create a new plan or copy the suite for the next release).
• Run the regression suite before each release candidate.
8. Traceability
• Requirement → Test Case: User Story "Tested By" test case links.
• Test Case → Bug: bugs created from the runner link automatically.
• Test Case → Automation: associate automated tests (Playwright, Selenium, etc.) through the test case's Associated Automation tab so pipeline runs update test points.
• Use the Requirements traceability report or query to confirm every story has linked cases and every failure has a bug.
9. Automation Linkage
1. Set Automation Status to Planned once a case is a candidate for automation.
2. After scripting, link the automated test method to the test case (Associated Automation).
3. Add a Visual Studio Test / Test Plan task in the CI/CD pipeline to run test cases by plan and suite, so results post back to the test points.
4. Set Automation Status to Automated after the first stable run.
