11. Entry and Exit Criteria
Entry criteria
• Story has approved acceptance criteria
• Test cases are in Ready state and peer reviewed
• Build is deployed to the target environment and smoke test passes
• Test data and access are available
Exit criteria
• 100% of planned test points executed
• All Priority 1 and 2 cases passed
• No open Severity 1 or 2 defects; remaining defects triaged and accepted
• Traceability confirmed for all in-scope stories
• QA Lead sign-off recorded
12. Maintenance and Governance
• Review and prune regression cases each quarter; move obsolete cases to Closed.
• Update test cases in the same sprint as the story change that affects them.
• Keep tags and naming consistent; the QA Lead audits quarterly.
• Do not delete executed test cases; close them to preserve history.
