14. Shared Parameters
The Parameters page in the Test Plans menu holds shared parameter sets that many test cases can reuse, instead of re-entering the same data in every case.
1. Go to Test Plans → Parameters and select New shared parameter set.
2. Name the set by data domain (e.g., Member Types, User Roles, Browsers) and add columns and rows.
3. In a test case, open the Parameter values section and choose Add existing shared parameters to link the set.
4. Update the shared set once and every linked test case picks up the change.
Use shared parameters for data reused across suites. Use local parameters (@name in steps) for data that belongs to a single case.
