16. Exploratory Sessions
Exploratory sessions captures unscripted testing alongside planned cases.
• Use it for new features, bug hunts, and areas with thin scripted coverage.
• Start a session against a work item or suite; ADO records screenshots, notes, and actions as you test.
• Create bugs, tasks, or test cases directly from findings during the session.
• Write a short charter first: Explore [area] with [data/role] to discover [risk], with a time box of 60 to 90 minutes.
• Promote valuable findings to scripted test cases and tag them regression.
17. Applying This to Your Current Suites
Your plan currently shows a suite for managing urgent members at 0% run. To bring it in line with this guide:
1. Rename the suite to <Story ID> – <Story Title> and convert it to a requirement-based suite if it is a static one.
2. Confirm each case is in Ready state, carries a priority, and has tags such as regression or negative.
3. Assign testers and configurations on the Execute tab so test points are generated.
4. Move repeated login or member-lookup steps into Shared Steps, and shared data (member types, roles) into Shared Parameters.
5. Run the smoke subset first, then the full suite, and review the Progress report daily.
